-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Game Over 2 (aka Phantis), part 2
  Publisher   Dinamic, 1988
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Game Over 2 (1988)(Dinamic)(ES)(en)(Part 2 of 2)[aka
              Phantis][re-release].z80
  MD5         55c89bb16ffde2f58a43ed3be7b95bcf

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures are drawn on the Next's own graphics layers, so they keep their
  own colours and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is
  unchanged.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: figures in their own colours on a double-buffered Layer 2,
              in the game's own plot order, over the original bitmap; scenery
              in its own attributes; the plot and the copy run whole at 28 MHz
              in pace windows; the tape's loading screen; Sinclair's 48K ROM
              as the whole alt ROM (NextZXOS 26.11 safe); the game's speed
              restored after every hook; R kept as the original's

  Note        Keys: first type the access code part 1 gives, 18757, then
              ENTER; then K keyboard (it asks for the keys), J Kempston
              joystick, S start; hold the key a moment. The original look:
              figures keep their own colours and the scenery its own. In the
              original the rocks around every figure turned its colour. Each
              figure's ink is on Layer 2, in the game's own order, over the
              original bitmap. Game Over 2, the English release of Phantis:
              English text, so no language set. Fits a 1MB Next. Known issues:
              pace in JNext -1.73 to +0.33% against the original over 800
              updates, 5 seeds; quiet thirds -1.29 to +0.06%, busy thirds
              -1.05 to +2.09%; slowest 20 updates +6.08%. Missing: Enhanced
              (no Spec256 set for part 2); natural play to the end; hardware
              untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Skip the access code

  The archive's POKEs for this release, tested alone in the simulator, same
  keys with and without: Infinite lives (lives never fall; 2 and 1 lost
  without it, 2 seeds), Skip the access code (the code screen is gone). The
  archive's [es] entries are for the Spanish release.

