  Tested      Run by script through the real loader on a NextZXOS 26.11 card
              copy; 1.0 not yet played by the owner; published at his request

  Replay      4 scripted recordings, 46063 frames: 44436 hooks run original
              and build from one state each: every register including R, all
              48K RAM but the changed bytes and the stack below SP, the
              attributes the copy wrote against the clean buffer: IDENTICAL;
              11192 Layer 2 pictures, 4958859 pixels, against an independent
              model and against the work bitmap: IDENTICAL; 10 broken builds
              caught; 320 ABI cases, each hook entered at all 4 CPU speeds,
              both IFF values, 8 R phases; the start-up exact with and without
              NEXLOAD

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: through the real .NEXCLASH loader on a
              private NextZXOS 26.11 card copy, output byte for byte as nxc.py
              makes it, reaching play; 15-minute soak against the original;
              flicker check clean; the overlay published outside the play
              area's rows

  Coverage    Scripted input, no human play: code screen, menu, play, deaths,
              game over; not reached: the later scenes beyond those the test
              copy met, natural completion

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
